cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Research engineering project, Miva Open University, supervised by
  Dr. Chukwuemeka Odi Agwu. Release v0.2.0 reports run r2026-11-13 in
  docs/RESULTS.md. If you use a number measured here, please cite this repository at
  the release the number appears in.
title: >-
  Development of a Calibration-Aware UAV Path Planning Model for Efficient Crop Disease
  Detection Under Limited Battery Capacity
abstract: >-
  Informative path planning assumes the information signal it consumes is calibrated.
  Deep classifiers are systematically miscalibrated and degrade further under
  distribution shift. This repository couples a fine-tuned crop-disease classifier's
  calibrated uncertainty to a reinforcement learning path planner for a UAV under an
  energy budget, and measures how calibration error propagates into planner
  performance. Temperature scaling holds accuracy fixed while confidence varies,
  isolating calibration as the independent variable.
authors:
